# Equinox Frontend Rules

## Design

Build a professional business application.

Prioritize:

* clarity
* speed
* readability
* consistent spacing
* keyboard usability
* responsive design

Avoid unnecessary animations.

## Forms

Forms should:

* clearly label fields
* show validation errors
* preserve entered values when possible
* disable duplicate submissions
* show saving/loading states
* clearly distinguish editable and read-only fields

## Transaction Forms

Fields inherited from previous documents should be visually identifiable as read-only.

Examples:

Invoice:

* Customer ID: hidden/internal
* Customer Name: read-only
* Item Name: read-only
* Sales Order reference: read-only

ATW/DR:

* Customer ID: hidden/internal
* Customer Name: read-only
* Invoice ID: read-only
* Item Name: read-only

Withdrawal Slip:

* Customer ID: hidden/internal
* Customer Name: read-only
* Invoice ID: read-only
* ATW/DR ID: read-only
* Item Name: read-only

## Tables

Transaction line-item tables should support:

* adding items
* editing permitted fields
* deleting draft lines
* quantity validation
* calculated amounts
* totals

## Destructive Actions

Cancellation and other destructive actions require confirmation.

Never use browser `alert()` for normal business interactions.

Use consistent modal/dialog components.

## Responsive Design

The application must work on:

* desktop
* laptop
* tablet
* mobile

Warehouse workflows should be particularly usable on mobile devices.

## Accessibility

Use semantic HTML.

Ensure:

* keyboard navigation
* visible focus states
* readable labels
* accessible dialogs
* appropriate ARIA attributes where required

Do not use color alone to communicate status.
